# leakguard (quench)

## Path Neutralization

NEVER output or commit host drive letters (`C:\`, `F:\`) or user profile directories (`Users/`, `/home/`).
Always use generic placeholders (`/path/to/<project>`, `~/.config/<tool>/`) or relative paths (`./config.json`).
Never mix forward and backward slashes in paths; use `/` universally across platforms.

## Hermetic Project Isolation

Maintain strict project isolation: never leak private tools, MCP names, internal APIs,
or sibling project names from the host environment into repository files, docs, or commits.
Every repository must be self-contained; only reference tools and dependencies defined locally.

## Secret Redaction

NEVER commit or output authentication tokens (`ghp_*`, `github_pat_*`, `sk-*`, `bearer *`)
or database connection strings with embedded passwords. Use environment variables.
